.page-section.p-120-cont.cg-section.grey-light-bg.clearfix(id="case-studies")
    .container
        .row
            .col-md-10.col-md-offset-1.text-center.mb-60
                h2.cg-section-title Representative case studies
                p.cg-section-lead Anonymized examples reflecting common engagement patterns. Your architecture and numbers will differ; the approach is the same.
        .row
            .col-md-4
                .cg-case-card.wow.fadeIn
                    h3 B2B SaaS — runaway Lambda bill
                    p
                        strong Problem.
                        |  Monthly AWS spend jumped 3x after a traffic milestone. Lambda concurrency, API Gateway, and outbound data dominated; no single owner for cost.
                    p
                        strong Solution.
                        |  Cost audit, concurrency and memory tuning, API caching, and removal of redundant cross-region traffic. Documented guardrails for future changes.
                    p.mb-0
                        strong Result.
                        |  ~32% infrastructure cost reduction within one billing cycle; p95 API latency improved ~40% from fewer duplicate calls.
            .col-md-4
                .cg-case-card.wow.fadeIn(data-wow-delay='150ms')
                    h3 Growth-stage API — timeouts at peak
                    p
                        strong Problem.
                        |  Core Go service looked fine in staging but 5xx and tail latency spiked under production concurrency.
                    p
                        strong Solution.
                        |  Production profiling, query and batching fixes, bounded worker pools, and queue-backed offload for non-critical work.
                    p.mb-0
                        strong Result.
                        |  p99 latency ~60% lower at peak; error rate dropped below prior SLO; team gained a repeatable load profile for releases.
            .col-md-4
                .cg-case-card.wow.fadeIn(data-wow-delay='300ms')
                    h3 Legacy monolith — slow, risky deploys
                    p
                        strong Problem.
                        |  Single deployable blocked feature teams; scaling meant bigger instances; incident recovery was manual.
                    p
                        strong Solution.
                        |  Strangled high-churn domains into Lambda handlers and event buses; kept transactional core with clear boundaries and observability.
                    p.mb-0
                        strong Result.
                        |  Deploy frequency moved from bi-weekly to multiple times per week for migrated surfaces; on-call pages for that domain dropped sharply.
